A1. This closes tight when you make a touch. (No, it isn't a Scotchman.) ~ CLAM
A5. What she did when she got tired of refusing you. ~ CEDED
A10. How a mother-in-law should be to be agreeable. ~ AFAR
A14. This is held in church. ~ RITE
A15. Another way to undo a mistake. ~ AMEND
A16. This is a howl, and how! ~ RAVE
A17. Wild stuff about the younger generation. ~ OATS
A18. What the Boston censors do to all the forbidden books. ~ READ
A19. When these become attached to you they are pretty hard to shake off. ~ NAMES
A20. This has been put away for safe keeping. ~ PRISONER
A22. Here is where little Bob came from. ~ ROBERT
A23. This goes into the makings of a maiden's hope-chest. ~ CEDAR
A24. A man of few words. ~ MUTE
A25. Sky pilot (abbr.). ~ DD
A27. The circus barker. ~ DOG
A28. This is what most bed-time stories are. ~ FABULOUS
A32. This kind of bow is seen in the best circles. ~ ARC
A34. A Mexican has-been. ~ REBEL
A36. Political funds. ~ SLUSH
A37. A beastly squawk. ~ ROAR
