A66. He put on the hottest show in town. ~ NERO
A67. A friend in need. ~ ALLY
A68. These embrace many forms. ~ BELTS
A69. This has a noiseless bark. ~ TREE

D1. This will keep the farmers guessing. ~ CROP
D2. The guy who wrote ". . . and they lived happily ever after." ~ LIAR
D3. This place is always full of memories of bygone days. ~ ATTIC
D4. Here is how our soldiers ate during the war. ~ MESSED
D5. These are wholesale killings. ~ CARNAGES
